<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 12+ backup/transfer rules (android:dataExtractionRules). Same
  root-cause fix as backup_rules.xml, for both cloud backup and device-to-device
  transfer: never carry the flutter_secure_storage EncryptedSharedPreferences
  file across installs/devices, because its Keystore decryption key does not come
  with it — a restored ciphertext then fails with BadPaddingException/BAD_DECRYPT.
  The app re-provisions these keys from the server on next launch instead.
-->

<!--
  [AVADIAL-BACKUP-RESTOREFIRST 2026-07-15] `cache/` (DiskCache — getFilesDir()/cache)
  is excluded too, and it is NOT a tidy-up: carrying it across devices actively
  destroys contacts.

  DiskCache is, by its own contract, "everything here is a cache re-fetched from the
  server". Auto Backup did not know that and restored it onto the new handset, which
  made two device-LOCAL facts lie about the new phone:

    • `ava_contact_backup_server_ts` ("this device has already uploaded") — the
      restore-first hold reads this to decide whether an automatic upload is safe.
      Restored onto a new phone it says "yes, we've synced here before", so the
      hold opens and the ~4s auto-sync replaces the user's cloud backup with the new
      handset's book BEFORE they ever tap Restore. The backup is destroyed by the
      backup feature, on the "I lost my phone" path it exists to serve.
    • `contacts_backup_master_uid` ("who owns this handset's phone book") — restored
      onto a new phone it names the OLD phone's owner, so someone who was a sub on a
      shared phone stays a sub on the phone they just bought, and their own address
      book silently never backs up.

  Both are statements about a HANDSET. They must not survive a change of handset.
  Excluding the cache costs a re-fetch on first launch, which is what a cache is for.
-->
<!--
  [AVA-BACKUP-EXCL-1 2026-08-07] `domain="file" path="."` — the WHOLE app-support
  root — is excluded. Keep this in step with backup_rules.xml.

  WHY. Ava's on-device brain is NOT a separate file: `core/local_brain/local_index.dart`
  and `core/ava_memory/*` create their tables with raw SQL on the SAME per-account
  drift connection as the messenger, i.e. inside
  `getApplicationSupportDirectory()/avatok_<AccountScope.id>.sqlite`
  (`core/db.dart` `_open()`, mirrored by `features/ava_backup/backup_service.dart:212`).
  On Android `getApplicationSupportDirectory()` IS `context.getFilesDir()`, which is
  exactly the `file` backup domain — so Auto Backup was uploading the brain, every
  decrypted DM, and the local memory index to Google in the clear.

  WHY THE WHOLE DOMAIN AND NOT ONE FILENAME. The `path` attribute of an
  `<exclude>` is a literal file or directory prefix — Android supports NO wildcards
  and no globs here. The DB name embeds the Clerk account id (`avatok_<scope>.sqlite`),
  which is not knowable at build time, so `avatok_*.sqlite` cannot be written. There
  is no targeted form of this rule; the domain root is the only expression of it.

  AND IT IS THE RIGHT SCOPE ANYWAY. Everything else under that root is either a
  cache or the same class of unencrypted private content: `media/<scope>/` holds
  DECRYPTED DM media, `callrec/<scope>/` call recordings, `lib_thumbs/`,
  `avavision_snapshots/`, `avatars/`, `ringtones/`, `media_outbox/`, plus
  `ava_models/` (a re-downloadable embedder model). None of it should leave the
  device un-encrypted, and none of it needs to: AvaTOK ships its OWN encrypted
  backup/restore (`features/ava_backup/backup_service.dart`), which is the
  supported way to carry this data to a new phone.

  Nothing is lost that was usable before: `FlutterSecureStorage.xml` is already
  excluded below, so a restored DB would have arrived on the new handset with no
  Keystore key to read anything with.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureStorage.xml"/>
        <!-- [AVA-BACKUP-EXCL-1] app-support root: brain DB + decrypted media. -->
        <exclude domain="file" path="."/>
        <exclude domain="file" path="cache/"/>
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureStorage.xml"/>
        <!-- [AVA-BACKUP-EXCL-1] app-support root: brain DB + decrypted media. -->
        <exclude domain="file" path="."/>
        <exclude domain="file" path="cache/"/>
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
